------------------------------------- List of races ---------------------------------------------------

- CREATE A NEW COMPONENT TO DISPLAY THE LIST OF RACES.

- Instructions:

1️⃣ Create a new component races which will allow to display the list of pony races.

        ng generate component races
    
    👉 Our new component should have a signal races containing an array of the races to display.
    
    👉To represent a race, we will create a TypeScript interface in a new folder models (inside app).
    Define this interface RaceModel in a file named race-model.ts. It should have two fields id, of
    type number, and name, of type string.

        ng generate interface models/race-model 
    
    Don’t forget to export it, so you can import it later.


2️⃣ In the component Races, start by initializing the races signal with a hard-coded, fake list of
    races:

        [{ id: 1, name: 'Lyon' }, { id: 2, name: 'London' }];


3️⃣ In the template, use a for loop to display this list of races. For each race, we want a div
    containing a h2 header containing the name of the race.


4️⃣ To display our component, add it in the template of the main component, just below the title.
    In order to validate the exercise, make sure all the unit tests provided in races.spec.ts are
    passing.